# Credentials and overrides for fleet. NEVER commit this file.
#   chmod 600 .env
#
# Values are read LITERALLY: no quoting required, no shell expansion performed.
# `bin/fleet` PARSES this file line by line rather than sourcing it, because a
# credential is not shell. A router password containing a bare `&` once aborted
# every fleet run, cron included; a value containing $(...) would have executed.
# If you add a loader anywhere else, parse it — never `set -a; . .env`.
#
# Layout: provider credentials, then device credentials, then optional overrides.
# Alphabetical within each section. Keep .env and .env.example in the same order
# so a diff between them shows what you are missing, not how you sorted it.


# ─────────────────────────────────────────────── provider credentials
# Only the providers you actually use need a value. An empty or absent entry is
# fine; `fleet` raises a named error when it needs one it does not have.

# DigitalOcean — API → Tokens (write scope).
DIGITALOCEAN_TOKEN=

# Fornex — Client area ("personal cabinet") after registration; there is NO API
# endpoint that mints these, so the web UI is the only source. Header format is
#   Authorization: Api-Key <prefix>.<secret>
# TWO THINGS TO DO BEFORE A DRIVER CAN WORK, both with lead time:
#   1. POST /orders/vps/ is DISABLED BY DEFAULT — "contact tech support to get
#      access" (/my/tickets/new/). Open that ticket early; without it Fornex can
#      only ever be a hand-rented `manual` node.
#   2. Creating a VPS via API bills from ACCOUNT BALANCE, so the balance must be
#      topped up first or the call fails.
# AS48040, 22-prefix ASN, ~EUR 4.68/mo, ~2x lower latency than Hetzner SIN.
FORNEX_API_KEY=

# Hetzner Cloud — Project → Security → API tokens (read+write).
# Singapore lands in AS215859, which is the measured-good one; the German
# estate is AS24940 and fails outright. See inventory.toml.
HCLOUD_TOKEN=

# SporeStack — this token is BOTH the credential and the wallet. Treat it like
# cash: whoever holds it can spend the balance. Generate one with
#   curl -s https://api.sporestack.com/token
SPORESTACK_TOKEN=

# UpCloud — Control Panel → Account → API Tokens → Add new API token.
# Starts `ucat_`, shown ONCE at creation, expires in at most 365 days.
# Leave "Allow token to create tokens" OFF: nothing here needs it, and it
# turns a cheaply-revocable credential into one that can mint siblings.
# Leave the IP allowlist OPEN: fleet sends provider API calls through
# FLEET_API_PROXY, so they egress from the CURRENT EXIT, and exits rotate
# every <=72h — an allowlist would pass once, then fail silently.
UPCLOUD_API_TOKEN=

# Vultr — Account → API → Personal Access Token. Note Vultr DOES enforce an
# IP allowlist on the token; see the note above about rotating exit IPs.
VULTR_API_KEY=

# Legacy UpCloud auth: HTTP Basic, `username:password` of a dedicated API
# sub-account. Still honoured when UPCLOUD_API_TOKEN is unset. Prefer the token.
# UPCLOUD_API_CREDENTIALS=


# ─────────────────────────────────────────────── device credentials
# Not providers. These are local/LAN devices, used only from the machine running
# fleet, and are never sent to any third party.

# MikroTik RB951Ui-2HnD — the upstream router in front of the Beryl.
# `admin` at 192.168.88.1. Kept here rather than pasted into a chat window.
# Day to day you should not need it: `ssh mikrotik` uses key auth (see the
# Host block in ~/.ssh/config). This is the fallback if the key stops working.
MIKROTIK_PASS=


# ─────────────────────────────────────────────── optional overrides
# All commented out by default. Uncomment only when you mean it.

# Send provider API calls through a proxy. Normally set from inventory.toml as
# `router.api_proxy`; this variable OVERRIDES that. It exists because TSPU freezes
# TLS uploads past ~12-20 KB and a server-create request carries ~11 KB of
# cloud-init, so `fleet rotate` fails on the bare line. SSH is unaffected.
# FLEET_API_PROXY=http://192.168.8.1:1080

# Restrict SSH on newly-created nodes to these sources. Unset means 0.0.0.0/0.
# The cheapest hardening available IF you have a static address — you do not, on
# CGNAT. Note the value is written into /etc/fleet.env on the node and sourced
# there, so it is shlex-quoted; the comma-space form below is safe.
# FLEET_SSH_ALLOW_V4=203.0.113.4/32, 198.51.100.0/24

# Verbose fleet logging. Same as passing -v.
# FLEET_VERBOSE=1

# Route the SporeStack API over Tor. Needs torsocks wrapping the process.
# SPORESTACK_USE_TOR_ENDPOINT=1
